EO:12543,FRDOC:E6-21005,E6-21005,Proposed Rule,2006-12-11,71 FR 71500,termination,ending,True,False,False,True,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2006/12/11/E6-21005.txt,ef54ce7e2eb469e05deb26ad97a2d8b5f56d94bf593e9039f1241b7e2e901be8,"Effective September 21, 2004, Executive Order 13357 terminated the national emergency declared in Executive Order 12543 of January 7, 1986, with respect to the policies and actions of the Government of Libya and revoked Executive Orders 12543, 12544 of January 8, 1986, and 12801 of April 15, 1992 (all of which had imposed sanctions against Libya in response to the national emergency)."
EO:12549,EO:13904,2020-02439,Presidential Document,2020-02-05,85 FR 6725,suspension,modifying,True,False,False,True,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/02/05/2020-02439.txt,b713a5b74cb449f658c0087ee7b2b8d665913e0f0209858397fb10cbf0cdf80b,"It is the policy of the United States Government, as reflected in Executive Order 12549 of February 18, 1986 (Debarment and Suspension), and elsewhere, to protect the public interest and ensure the integrity of Federal programs by transacting only with presently responsible persons."
