EO:12928,FRDOC:97-1093,97-1093,Notice,1997-01-16,62 FR 2358,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1997/01/16/97-1093.txt,b2c3d33f1a71db1312dbb0e58b7337cbcafef0483a25d3c96a03760c2ae032b1,This collection of information is necessary to implement the reporting requirements of Executive Order 12928.
EO:12928,FRDOC:97-6309,97-6309,Rule,1997-03-17,62 FR 12690,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1997/03/17/97-6309.txt,35147106f8960fc1341d73c94f8c7c850abbbc8eb8783eefcc43442fb4136f7d,"This final rule adds a new FAR Subpart 26.3 and a new solicitation provision at 52.226-2 to implement Executive Order 12928, which requires agencies to provide periodic reporting on the progress made in award of contracts to Historically Black Colleges and Universities and Minority Institutions."
EO:12928,FRDOC:97-6316,97-6316,Rule,1997-03-17,62 FR 12702,amendment,modifying,True,False,False,,4,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1997/03/17/97-6316.txt,657333f036ca4f94540ff9ceed990113e08cf19b38ab81604af11acb6f2c3a71,"SUMMARY: The Civilian Agency Acquisition Council and the Defense Acquisition Regulations Council have agreed on a final rule amending the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) to implement Executive Order 12928, which requires agencies to provide periodic reporting on the progress made in award of contracts to Historically Black Colleges and Universities and Minority Institutions."
EO:12928,FRDOC:97-6324,97-6324,Rule,1997-03-17,62 FR 12721,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1997/03/17/97-6324.txt,0b73fa417349598e3d18bacee2b3e387be0a52e031943d0e0a7b653350f12cd6,"This final rule adds a new FAR Subpart 26.3 and a new solicitation provision at 52.226-2 to implement Executive Order 12928, which requires agencies to provide periodic reporting on the progress made in award of contracts to Historically Black Colleges and Universities and Minority Institutions."
