EO:13920,FRDOC:2020-14668,2020-14668,Notice,2020-07-08,85 FR 41023,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,17,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/07/08/2020-14668.txt,c5d3e2c0c31cf1a33884b15f54b87ef776cc33a8ffdb5b2645315375981deb96,"SUMMARY: Pursuant to Executive Order 13920 (E.O. 13920) issued May 1, 2020, titled ``Securing the United States Bulk-Power System,'' the Department of Energy (DOE or the Department) is seeking information to understand the energy industry's current practices to identify and mitigate vulnerabilities in the supply chain for components of the bulk-power system (BPS)."
EO:13920,FRDOC:2020-15848,2020-15848,Notice,2020-07-21,85 FR 44061,extension,modifying,True,False,False,,2,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/07/21/2020-15848.txt,f4c032b8a3a9fe52e0af1815e4d710073354c17a85d09f0a419fcab795546d3e,"SUMMARY: The U.S. Department of Energy (``DOE'') is extending the public comment period for its Request for Information (``RFI'') regarding Executive Order 13920 (E.O. 13920) issued May 1, 2020, titled ``Securing the United States Bulk-Power System.'' DOE published the RFI in the Federal Register on July 8, 2020, establishing a 30-day public comment period that will end on August 7, 2020."
EO:13920,FRDOC:2020-28773,2020-28773,Notice,2021-01-06,86 FR 533,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,17,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/01/06/2020-28773.txt,342f0116dd275e2fd7537a67cd30c92180e0b0d4a4f51983df5a47907d21cfd0,"SUMMARY: The U.S. Department of Energy (Department or DOE) gives notice of this Prohibition Order prohibiting the acquisition, importation, transfer, or installation of specified bulk-power system (BPS) electric equipment that directly serves Critical Defense Facilities (CDFs), pursuant to Executive Order 13920."
EO:13920,EO:13990,2021-01765,Presidential Document,2021-01-25,86 FR 7037,suspension,modifying,True,False,False,True,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/01/25/2021-01765.txt,dd37f4ac69192da14c0e7501cb34acb70ea128fa580b51491d30bdeb47e98cf4,"(c) Executive Order 13920 of May 1, 2020 (Securing the United States Bulk-Power System), is hereby suspended for 90 days."
EO:13920,FRDOC:2021-08482,2021-08482,Notice,2021-04-22,86 FR 21309,suspension,modifying,True,False,False,,8,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/04/22/2021-08482.txt,f84d3d5d5b07590d4548c3775ff7f7da6a8d77122b3a37d677187c0fbcef3042,"On January 20, 2021, Executive Order 13990, Protecting Public Health and the Environment and Restoring Science to Tackle the Climate Crisis, was issued, which suspended E.O. 13920 for 90 days.\9\ As the December 2020 Prohibition Order is predicated on the authorities delegated to DOE by E.O. 13920, the Prohibition Order was also suspended during this same time period."
EO:13920,FRDOC:2021-08483,2021-08483,Notice,2021-04-22,86 FR 21308,revocation,ending,True,False,False,,6,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/04/22/2021-08483.txt,11f970180c286ce9cc23c3b94acd35e73498210e970d205260f033519e36fb3e,"The Department is revoking the December 2020 Prohibition Order effective April 20, 2021, in order to create a stable policy environment before the emergency declaration made by E.O. 13920 expires on May 1, 2021, and while the Department conducts a Request for Information to develop a strengthened and administrable strategy to address the security of the U.S. energy sector."
